<article class="env-theorem" id="039Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039Q">Theorem <span data-tag="039Q">41.13.1</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \in X$. If $\varphi $ is smooth at $x$, then there exist an integer $n \geq 0$ and affine opens $V \subset Y$ and $U \subset X$ with $x \in U$ and $\varphi (U) \subset V$ such that there exists a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[d] &  U \ar[l] \ar[d] \ar[r]_-\pi &  \mathbf{A}^ n_ R \ar[d] \ar@{=}[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]) \ar[dl] \\  Y &  V \ar[l] \ar@{=}[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R) }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\pi $ is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/054L" data-tag="054L">29.37.21</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>